WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.350
The help desk executes approved work.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.550
It never decides what it executes.

3
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.146
Technicians hold no standing admin roles;

4
00:00:07.146 --> 00:00:10.188
they switch on a scoped role
for the ticket in hand.

5
00:00:10.188 --> 00:00:13.900
The book flags a trap:
capability isn't authority.

6
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.181
Some roles a help desk
might hold can delete users

7
00:00:17.181 --> 00:00:20.462
or approve app access, which
the desk must never do.

8
00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:25.162
Executive accounts sit in a protected
unit the general desk can't touch.

9
00:00:25.162 --> 00:00:29.650
And security monitoring flags any
elevation with no matching ticket.

10
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.623
The decision for the
identity governance officer:

11
00:00:32.623 --> 00:00:37.012
scope the desk's privileged group, and
review its membership every quarter.

12
00:00:37.012 --> 00:00:39.410
Next, the tasks that need more.
